{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1333728-frost-fire-and-mountain-giants","id":1333728,"title":"Frost, Fire, and Mountain Giants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-02T13:12:53-07:00","id":1333728,"title":"Frost, Fire, and Mountain Giants","content":"I have a great love for the mythologies and folklore of many cultures and I generally try to base the characters I create for Beat as well as Changeling on mythical monsters and humanoids found therein. That being said, I am wondering what your opinions would be on which hungers best fit one of the 3 main giant species found in Norse mythology? I personally have Fire Giants as Anakim/Ravagers and the Frost/Mountain Giants as Anakim/Tyrants. Would you think that Frost and Mountain Giants could also be Ravagers or of another hunger altogether?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T13:35:08-07:00","id":1333730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darklander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1333728-frost-fire-and-mountain-giants#post1333728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a great love for the mythologies and folklore of many cultures and I generally try to base the characters I create for Beat as well as Changeling on mythical monsters and humanoids found therein. That being said, I am wondering what your opinions would be on which hungers best fit one of the 3 main giant species found in Norse mythology? I personally have Fire Giants as Anakim/Ravagers and the Frost/Mountain Giants as Anakim/Tyrants. Would you think that Frost and Mountain Giants could also be Ravagers or of another hunger altogether?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the initial problem with this question is that in the mythology giants are... for lack of a better word, people as well as monsters - they vary. The giant(s?) that built Asgard's walls might be taken for a Collector, given their desire to claim Freya, while Surtr is unquestionably a Ravager. Utgard-Loki strikes me as an Anakim Tyrant, given his desire to belittle Thor, Loki and the human companion whose name escapes me.<br /> <br /> All of this aside, I do find it interesting how the word <i>jotunn</i> is thought to have had its etymological roots in 'consuming', 'voracious/gluttonous' or 'greedy'. Very fitting for Beasts, given that you <i>could</i> translate 'jotunn' as 'devourer' or similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}